@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.large.file.attachment"

Feature: Zendesk Large File Attachment
	Testing the large file uploader in Zendesk.

Scenario: Download large file as customer
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Customer users should not be able to download large attached files that they own if they are flaged as No Personal Content

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I assign the web user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code        | LFAZENLFAZEN                  | |
	| Data Region | United States                 | |
	| Language    | English                       | |
	| Name        | Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region      | United States                 | |
	| Status      | Active                        | |
	| Tier        | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "LFAZENLFAZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	Then I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I download attached file "Document_1.txt" on position "1"
	And I download the attached file "Document_1.txt" on request details
	And I should see the downloaded file "Document_1.txt"
	And I should see the downloaded file "Document_1 (1).txt"
	When I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_2.txt      |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment  |
	| Data Region      | United States       |
	| No Personal Data | true                |
	Then I download the attached large file "Document_2.txt" with the comment "Large File Comment"
	And I should not see the downloaded file "Document_2.txt"
	And I go to the request with the ID "${staticRequestId}"
	When I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_3.txt      |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment  |
	| Data Region      | United States       |
	| No Personal Data | false               |
	Then I download the attached large file "Document_3.txt" with the comment "Large File Comment"
	And I should not see the downloaded file "Document_3.txt"

Scenario: Download employee large file as a customer
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Customer users should not be able to download large attached files uploaded by an employee

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I assign the web user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	And I assign the web user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the web organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And I assign the web user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code        | LFAZENLFAZEN                  | |
	| Data Region | United States                 | |
	| Language    | English                       | |
	| Name        | Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region      | United States                 | |
	| Status      | Active                        | |
	| Tier        | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "LFAZENLFAZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	Then I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	Then I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	Then I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the request with the ID "${staticRequestId}"
	And I accept all cookies
	When I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_2.txt     |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment |
	| Data Region      | United States      |
	| No Personal Data | true               |
	And I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_3.txt     |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment |
	| Data Region      | United States      |
	| No Personal Data | false              |
	Then I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the request with the ID "${staticRequestId}"
	And I accept all cookies
	And I download attached file "Document_1.txt" on position "3"
	And I download the attached file "Document_1.txt" on request details
	And I should see the downloaded file "Document_1.txt"
	And I should see the downloaded file "Document_1 (1).txt"
	And I download the attached large file "Document_2.txt" with the comment "Large File Comment"
	And I should not see the downloaded file "Document_2.txt"
	Then I go to the request with the ID "${staticRequestId}"
	And I download the attached large file "Document_3.txt" with the comment "Large File Comment"
	And I should not see the downloaded file "Document_3.txt"

